A trainer has a purse (money) and a partner (text, if any).
A move has a power (number) and an owner (trainer).
A move can be quick.
A move is strong when its power is at least 40.
The rating of a move is its power * 2.
A trainer's purse is never less than $0.
A move's power is always at least 0.
A stance is one of attack, guard or switch.
For a stance, guard means "Stay in and defend."
There is a trainer called Red whose purse is $250.
There is a trainer called Brock whose purse is $100 and whose partner is "Onix".
There is a quick move called Scratch whose power is 40 and whose owner is Red.
There is a move called Bind whose owner is Brock, and whose power is 15.

